menu "Clock drift diagnostic"

    config DIAG_CLOCK_DRIFT
    bool "Measure the crystal against USB SOF and log satellite TX"
    default n
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
    help
        Prints DRIFT lines (crystal offset against the host's 1 kHz USB
        start-of-frame, plus die temperature) every window, a TX line for
        each satellite packet, and a HOP line for each of its frames with
        the frequency the radio was set to. Off in normal builds.

    config DIAG_CLOCK_DRIFT_WINDOW_S
    int "Measurement window, in seconds"
    default 5
    range 1 60
    depends on DIAG_CLOCK_DRIFT
    help
        Longer windows give finer ppm resolution and fewer samples.

    config DIAG_TX_START_DELAY_S
    int "Hold the first satellite packet until this many seconds after boot"
    default 0
    range 0 3600
    depends on DIAG_CLOCK_DRIFT
    help
        0 leaves TX timing as it is. Use it to see whether corrections
        follow time since power-on rather than the first transmissions.

endmenu
